EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Contested_Isle_Ulster_EinriMacCilliniMichDaireBoircech" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Contested Isle - Éinri mac Cillíni mich Dáire Boircech"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Contested_Isle_Core_Ext"

    # Éinri mac Cillíni mich Dáire Boircech (Chapter Nine: The Province of Ulster, p109): one character, its stat lines verbatim fields.

    #ted910247859fde12dce291 ^"Éinri mac Cillíni mich Dáire Boircech" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tcdf966f3dff3db195bc5f0 ^"Vigil"]
            ^"Age" STRING "95 (apparent age 60)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Welcoming +3, Boasting +2, Lordly +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Contested Isle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 109
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Though not the oldest magus at Vigil, Éinri mac Cillíni (AYN-rih moc KIL-leenih) is their leader; holder of the black pig’s tusks, master of the cattle, and keeper of the bees. He is a large, bearded, figure dressed in velvet robes and chains of silver and gold. He eats and drinks more than is good for his humors, resulting in attacks of gout. He invented a spell to provide some relief, but the spell is flawed and while it dulls the pain it does so at the expense of his mood, something Éinri puts down to his wife’s nagging.\n\nHis large court is the center of the covenant’s community, and an endless supply of silver ensures that his kitchens are full of cooks and his halls full of guests Hermetic, faerie, magical, and mundane. Éinri has a love for stories and is keen to hear tales from beyond Ireland. The honey produced by Éinri’s bees is widely acknowledged to be among the best in Hibernia, and Éinri makes frequent gifts of it to friends and allies.\n\nThanks to powerful longevity rituals, his wife Aoife has retained much of her youth and looks much younger than her husband. Éinri and Aoife have recently adopted a young boy into the court of Vigil, raising him as their own. Éinri intends to have him join House Mercere in due course, so may need to gain sponsorship from one of the Mercer Houses.\n\nÉinri’s talisman takes the form of a coat of bronze mail, enchanted such that it grows along with his girth. His familiar is a large, lazy wolf hound.\n\nÉinri has a long-running feud with Dalton Ballaugh of Lámbaird. They have fought numerous certamen and their grogs have frequently clashed. It has not yet escalated to Wizard War, but the magi loathe each other. Onlookers may find this animosity strange given the similarity between the men and their covenants, but perhaps therein lies the problem."
    }

}
